d and  because they've discovered that their  hospitals the icus are  nowhere near as full as they were with  the delta and the beta variant people  who were in hospital for delta and beta  for eight days have been in hospital for  three days with omicron the ventilators  are hardly being used so they found that  the hospitalizations and debts are much  much lower on the other hand there is no  running away from it this is hugely  infectious and and so they decided from  a practical point of view to change the  rules now we don't know exactly what  it's going to be now it will be  announced officially soon but i think  the way the direction things are heading  in now is recognizing that we've got to  live with the variance going forward in  a safer manner and practical a manner as  possible using lateral protests using  our world-leading booster program which  is fantastic we can protect our citizens  our businesses with two lines of defense  one is the vaccines next you have the  lateral flow testing the third that now  people are finally talking about we've  been calling out this since january is  having repurposed new treatments and the  antivirals for example the fisa  antiviral has shown in trials to reduce  deaths and hospitalizations by 89  once that becomes available that is a  game changer in that you treat people  they take the tablets for five days and  you reduce the hospitalization and death  so the combination of those things i  think is looking very optimistic ahead  we've got to get through this period  right now  you talk about the importance of mass  testing and the the valuable  contribution to that made by lateral  flow tests are you concerned at all that  we are getting warnings from pharmacists  today about the difficulty of of getting  hold of lateral flows in some areas  apache supply problems currently does  that worry you when everyone's building  up to go back to work after the  christmas and new year period  absolutely the government has got to do  everything it can to have these lateral  protests freely available just earlier  this month we ran out and that is not a  good situation to be in because the cost  of these natural blue tests if you put  that cost  into context of the billions it costs  when you restrict the economy even with  plan b let alone a lockdown those costs  it cost us 400 billion pounds to save  the economy and businesses and  livelihoods throughout this pandemic the  cost of having a huge supply of freely  available natural field tests to  businesses and to people in their homes  or to pick up from pharmacies is the  cost benefit is off the scales you just  must have as many lateral protests uh as  we can because they are shown now time  and again to be reliable  and helping to identify people who have  covered we must use them to the maximum  government must make them freely  available and continue to have them  freely available going forward at least  into the spring  lord bilamoria thanks so much for your  time interesting to talk to you thank  you  thank you
 

